      "_agent_explorer": "Error: Reached max turns (4)",
      "_agent_risk": "I'll investigate the stepper/multi-step form patterns in the enterprise app to identify what could cause data blanking between steps.",
      "_agent_requirements": "The bug is in the **enterprise application** (the app the agent generates code for), not in the agent's own UI. The description is extremely vague \u2014 no specific page, form, or reproduction steps provided. Here's what I can extract:\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements (from defect description)\n- **FR-1**: All form data entered on any step of a multi-step form/wizard MUST be preserved when navigating to the next step\n- **FR-2**: All form data entered on any step MUST be preserved when navigating back to a previous step\n- **FR-3**: Data persistence must be deterministic \u2014 \"sometimes, randomly\" indicates a race condition, stale closure, or improper state management that must be eliminated\n- **FR-4**: Step transitions (forward and backward) must not trigger unnecessary re-renders that reset local component state\n- **FR-5**: If step components are unmounted/remounted during navigation, their data must be restored from a shared parent state or store \u2014 not held in local `useState` alone\n\n### Business Rules\n- **BR-1**: Users must never lose entered data due to step navigation \u2014 partial data loss causes re-entry friction and potential submission errors\n- **BR-2**: The fix must apply to ALL multi-step forms in the enterprise app (not just one specific form)\n- **BR-3**: Enterprise product ID checks (`VITE_PRODUCT_ID`) must remain intact \u2014 no regression to other product lines\n\n### UI / UX Requirements\n- **UI-1**: No visible flicker or blank flash when transitioning between steps\n- **UI-2**: Returning to a previous step must show the exact data the user entered, including partially-filled fields\n- **UI-3**: Dropdown/select values, checkboxes, radio buttons, and text inputs must all persist equally\n\n### Likely Root Causes to Investigate\n- **RC-1**: Step components using local `useState` that resets on unmount/remount (most common cause)\n- **RC-2**: Race condition between `setState` and step transition \u2014 state update not committed before navigation fires\n- **RC-3**: `useEffect` with incorrect dependency array resetting form fields on re-render\n- **RC-4**: Controlled component losing its value source (e.g., parent state resets to `undefined`/`\"\"` during transition)\n- **RC-5**: Key prop changes on step container causing full component tree remount\n\n### Information Gaps (need from reporter)\n- **Which specific form(s)?** (e.g., invoice creation, GST return filing, configuration wizard)\n- **Which specific steps?** (step 1\u21922, 2\u21923, or going back?)\n- **Which fields go blank?** (all fields or specific ones?)\n- **Browser/device?** (could be a browser-specific issue)\n- **Reproducible frequency?** (\"randomly\" suggests intermittent \u2014 need exact reproduction steps)\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\nLift all step-level form data out of local component state and into a **shared parent state or Zustand store** keyed by step index. Each step component should read its initial values from this shared store on mount and write back on every change (or on blur/before-navigate). Use a single `formData` object at the wizard level rather than per-step `useState` calls. If steps are rendered via conditional `{activeStep === n && <StepN />}`, consider switching to `display: none` CSS toggling (keeps components mounted) or persisting to store before unmount via a `useEffect` cleanup. The \"random\" nature strongly suggests a race condition \u2014 check for async operations (API calls, debounced saves) that overwrite form state after navigation. Before implementing, the specific form(s) affected must be identified from the reporter to scope the fix accurately.",
      "_agent_analysis": "The bug is in the **enterprise application** (the app the agent generates code for), not in the agent's own UI. The description is extremely vague \u2014 no specific page, form, or reproduction steps provided. Here's what I can extract:\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements (from defect description)\n- **FR-1**: All form data entered on any step of a multi-step form/wizard MUST be preserved when navigating to the next step\n- **FR-2**: All form data entered on any step MUST be preserved when navigating back to a previous step\n- **FR-3**: Data persistence must be deterministic \u2014 \"sometimes, randomly\" indicates a race condition, stale closure, or improper state management that must be eliminated\n- **FR-4**: Step transitions (forward and backward) must not trigger unnecessary re-renders that reset local component state\n- **FR-5**: If step components are unmounted/remounted during navigation, their data must be restored from a shared parent state or store \u2014 not held in local `useState` alone\n\n### Business Rules\n- **BR-1**: Users must never lose entered data due to step navigation \u2014 partial data loss causes re-entry friction and potential submission errors\n- **BR-2**: The fix must apply to ALL multi-step forms in the enterprise app (not just one specific form)\n- **BR-3**: Enterprise product ID checks (`VITE_PRODUCT_ID`) must remain intact \u2014 no regression to other product lines\n\n### UI / UX Requirements\n- **UI-1**: No visible flicker or blank flash when transitioning between steps\n- **UI-2**: Returning to a previous step must show the exact data the user entered, including partially-filled fields\n- **UI-3**: Dropdown/select values, checkboxes, radio buttons, and text inputs must all persist equally\n\n### Likely Root Causes to Investigate\n- **RC-1**: Step components using local `useState` that resets on unmount/remount (most common cause)\n- **RC-2**: Race condition between `setState` and step transition \u2014 state update not committed before navigation fires\n- **RC-3**: `useEffect` with incorrect dependency array resetting form fields on re-render\n- **RC-4**: Controlled component losing its value source (e.g., parent state resets to `undefined`/`\"\"` during transition)\n- **RC-5**: Key prop changes on step container causing full component tree remount\n\n### Information Gaps (need from reporter)\n- **Which specific form(s)?** (e.g., invoice creation, GST return filing, configuration wizard)\n- **Which specific steps?** (step 1\u21922, 2\u21923, or going back?)\n- **Which fields go blank?** (all fields or specific ones?)\n- **Browser/device?** (could be a browser-specific issue)\n- **Reproducible frequency?** (\"randomly\" suggests intermittent \u2014 need exact reproduction steps)\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\nLift all step-level form data out of local component state and into a **shared parent state or Zustand store** keyed by step index. Each step component should read its initial values from this shared store on mount and write back on every change (or on blur/before-navigate). Use a single `formData` object at the wizard level rather than per-step `useState` calls. If steps are rendered via conditional `{activeStep === n && <StepN />}`, consider switching to `display: none` CSS toggling (keeps components mounted) or persisting to store before unmount via a `useEffect` cleanup. The \"random\" nature strongly suggests a race condition \u2014 check for async operations (API calls, debounced saves) that overwrite form state after navigation. Before implementing, the specific form(s) affected must be identified from the reporter to scope the fix accurately.\n\nError: Reached max turns (4)\n\nI'll investigate the stepper/multi-step form patterns in the enterprise app to identify what could cause data blanking between steps.",
